      <h2>About Mangapwani Slave Chambers</h2>
      <div>Mangapwani Slave Chambers on the northwest coast are hidden coral caves where enslaved people were illegally held after the 1873 abolition decree, awaiting clandestine transport to Arabia and Persia. The main chamber, a natural coral cave with a freshwater pool, and the adjacent artificial chamber carved into the cliff tell a somber but essential chapter of Zanzibar's history. Guided tours provide historical context on the East African slave trade, abolition efforts, and the site's archaeological significance. A reflective, educational experience.</div>
